Echo the parameters provided via param lines.

Context
- You will receive up to five lines before this directive content in the exact form:
  param1=<value>
  param2=<value>
  param3=<value>
  param4=<value>
  param5=<value>
- Some parameters may be missing or empty. Treat missing values as empty strings.

Task
- Output exactly five lines in this order, echoing the parameter values:
  param1: <value of param1>
  param2: <value of param2>
  param3: <value of param3>
  param4: <value of param4>
  param5: <value of param5>
- Always include all five lines even if some values are empty.
- Do not include any additional commentary, headers, code fences, or explanations.
- The output must be only those five lines.
